# Keeps the build context to actual source. Beyond the transfer cost, a
# `COPY frontend/ ./` or `COPY extension/ ./` from a working tree that has been
# built locally would drop the host's node_modules on top of the ones the image
# just installed — a Linux image running whatever binaries the host happened to
# have. Everything listed here is either rebuilt inside the image or belongs
# only to the machine it was created on.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules

# Produced by this image's own build stages
frontend/dist
extension/.output
extension/.wxt
backend/app/static
backend/app/extension_dist
plugin

# Local runtime state and secrets — .env especially: it holds the generated
# SECRET_KEY and database password, and must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.local
*.sqlite3
*.db
data
uploads
*.install.log

# Caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
